// Transition and add to place (M5, §13.3): “Select all the preloads/specializations... I
// want to add... and let it lie somewhere inside without messing with me.” The main thing
// is that I can contact him at any time... I can write foo(int) and go. The added overload
// is the internal element of the module: in the base and in the execution, but not in the
// presentation of the module.
//
// program: editor_overloads.tz
open_view module
// F12 on call: selected in instance - first, then all overload
pointer 1 @area:3 0 1
key 1 F12
// expect: items=⏎  name="area(i64 n)" kind="перегрузка" detail="выбрана здесь"
// expect: name="area(f64 x)" kind="перегрузка" detail=""
// Enter - function in the second panel (presentation fn)
key 1 Enter
// expect: view view=2
// expect: kind="fn"
// expect: текст:⏎area(i64 n) => n * n;
// Ctrl+P: Accurate by signature - first
goto 2 area(f64)
// expect: items=⏎  name="area(f64 x)" kind="перегрузка" detail="точно"
key 2 Escape
// No signature - "add" first
goto 2 area(str)
// expect: items=⏎  name="добавить area(str)" kind="добавить" detail="внутренняя перегрузка"
key 2 Enter
// parameter names - as in overload of the same arity; cursor - in the body
// expect: текст:⏎area(str n) {⏎  ⏎}
// expect: курсор:   ‸
// Module view has not changed - internal is not visible
// expect-not: update view=1
// editing
key 2 0
// expect: area(str n) {⏎  0⏎}
// body value survives the intermediate hole (`n.`)
key 2 Backspace
key 2 n
key 2 .
key 2 s
key 2 i
key 2 z
key 2 e
// expect: area(str n) {⏎  n.size⏎}
// call non-existent function - error in place; F12 - "add" for argument types over all
// instance
pointer 1 @area:4 0 0
key 1 End
key 1 Enter
key 1 l
key 1 a
key 1 b
key 1 e
key 1 l
key 1 (
key 1 x
key 1 s
key 1 .
key 1 s
key 1 i
key 1 z
key 1 e
key 1 )
key 1 ;
// expect: label(xs.size);
// expect: kind="error" text="неизвестная функция label(i64)
key 1 ArrowLeft
key 1 ArrowLeft
key 1 F12
// expect: items=⏎  name="добавить label(i64)" kind="добавить" detail="внутренняя перегрузка"
key 1 Enter
// expect: текст:⏎label(i64 a) {⏎  ⏎}
// There is no more error at the call site, the text of the module - without a label
// expect-not: kind="error"
